  "scope": "Existing generic_terminated_array nine-place source/runtime counterfactual review; no fresh R7 execution claim.",
  "findings": {
    "fact_transport": "Text carrying the same last-byte predicate travels through all nine places. Explicit Count4 and inferred Count calls borrow the complete bytes field. Field/parameter/results/const/nested and selected implementation paths all invoke the same verifier.",
    "runtime_lengths": "First array must yield3; early-NUL second array must yield1. Returning Count4 fails. Returning Count-1 or ignoring the early NUL fails the second oracle. Each explicit and inferred result is independently compared with the supplied expected value.",
    "match": "Both matching and wildcard paths execute and have distinguishable length3/1 results; swapping or collapsing arms traps.",
    "canaries": "The verifier checks Text prefix0xa5 and suffix0x5a alongside both lengths. Starting at prefix gives length4/2; starting one byte late gives2/0, rather than3/1. These are concrete discriminating errors, not proof against all possible layout bugs or nonmutating overreads.",
    "twins": "All nine positive/negative source diffs are exactly first array final byte0->1. Build files are unchanged. Actual intended refusal is Text literal default-domain violation; this tests construction enforcement, not a malformed value successfully reaching the CText call.",
    "formation_and_guards": "Count>0 precedes formation of text[Count-1]. Both boundary calls occur before the result/canary transition. Caller expected values are runtime oracles and cannot establish the earlier terminator premise.",
    "pins": "All18 positive/negative main and Build files byte-match their corresponding corpus pins.",
    "targets": "Four hosted native strlen bindings and ProgramEntry rows are present; target_body selects ordinary named implementations. Binding presence is not four-host execution evidence."
  },
